-- prosa.stzu -- Prosa, declared as a Haro language
--
-- GENERATED by haro/gen-prosa-stzu.js from Prosa's own data: the kinds, the measures and the zones of
-- tools/prosa/prosa.js, the summaries of conformance/violations.json, and a field table the generator keeps and
-- checks against the reference court on every run. Judged by the Haro meta-court and forged into a court:
--     haro haro.haro prosa.stzu             (haro/spike, the meta-court)
--     haro forge.haro prosa.stzu <out dir>  (haro/spike, the forge: prosa_court.haro and prosa.gbnf)
-- The reference court (tools/prosa/prosa.js) is unchanged and is not replaced by this file. This file declares what
-- the meta-language carries of Prosa; the SEAMS below count what it does not carry.
--
-- Words are lower_snake here and UPPER in a .proz file (STYLE, HOLDS): the meta-language reserves UPPER_SNAKE for its
-- own keywords, and Zayn made the same trade. A code a rule names (CODE LACK_LISTED) is a lower_snake name here.
--
-- SEAMS -- what the meta-language of 2026-11-26 does not carry, counted against violations.json (31 codes):
--   S1  the text: levels 3, 4 and 5 judge a written text against the declaration (14 codes of level 3, 1 of level 4,
--       and every code a style declares). A declared language judges declarations, so the text stays with prosa.js.
--   S2  one clause, one value: a clause of the Commons holds one value, and a Prosa field holds a run of values. A bound
--       (DASHES AT_MOST 4 PER_THOUSAND), a budget, FIRST 150 and each entry of REFUSES or MATCHES ("never" WITHIN 3 "run")
--       reach the court as one text, and a phrase list reaches it as a list of texts. The boundary is the judge's
--       translator. BAD_VALUE is carried for the four closed vocabularies (zones, positions, severities, mention
--       modes); the inner grammar of a bound and of an entry is not declared here, so DASHES SOMETIMES is judged clean.
--   S3  arithmetic: BOUND_INVERTED compares the two ends of a bound, and the condition language compares a seat with a
--       written number. It is not carried.
--   S4  the rule run on its own example: EXAMPLE_NOT_REFUSED and EXAMPLE_NOT_LAWFUL run a PATTERN on its REFUSED and
--       WRITTEN sentences. A condition is read and is never run, so the self-test stays with prosa.js.
--   S5  a match across declarations: TERM_REFUSED_AND_REQUIRED matches the word a TERM writes against the entries of
--       every other rule its style reaches through HOLDS and ADOPTS, less DECLINES. The condition language joins
--       declarations by name and has no test of a word against an entry.
--   S6  inheritance: EXTENDS holds one name, and the relation cyclic reads a list of references. A cycle of forms is
--       carried to three steps, written out, and PIECE_WITHOUT_SUBJECT reads the form a piece names and the form
--       that one extends, two steps. prosa.js follows EXTENDS to its end. A cycle of styles is carried whole by
--       ADOPTS cyclic.
--   S7  codes: UNKNOWN_FIELD is refused as UNKNOWN_CLAUSE, DUPLICATE_FIELD, UNEXPECTED_TOKEN and UNTERMINATED_STRING
--       as PARSE, and DUPLICATE_DECLARATION as DUPLICATE_NAME. Each is refused; the code spoken is the court's own.
--       A value of the wrong shape (a name where a text stands) is refused as PARSE and not as BAD_VALUE.
--   S8  the reader stops: a refusal of the reader of the court (PARSE, UNKNOWN_CLAUSE, UNKNOWN_KIND, DUPLICATE_NAME) ends the
--       judgment at the first one, and prosa.js reports every finding of level 1. The findings of the menus, the
--       constraints and the references are all reported, as prosa.js reports them.
--   S9  RATIONALE: the Commons makes RATIONALE mandatory on every declaration, and a .proz declaration has none. At
--       the boundary a declaration reaches the court with RATIONALE "none given". EVIDENCE is Prosa's own reason, and
--       it stays a seat.
--   S10 USE: a .proz file reads other files with USE, and names are global across them. The court judges one
--       sentence; the boundary hands it the files already joined.
--   S11 cites: violations.json binds a code to its invariant and to no rule, article, right or pattern. Each CITES
--       names the diagnostic itself (rule:<CODE>), the form the cite list of the meta-language accepts. The court
--       speaks UNKNOWN_KIND with an empty cite list: the CITES of unknown_declaration reach a NAMED word only.
--   S12 a universal field: EVIDENCE, CODE, SEVERITY, LANGUAGE, ON, IN, MENTIONS, KEEPS and SAYS belong to several
--       kinds, and the meta-language has no seat shared by kinds, so they repeat on each.
--   S13 open words: TITLE_HOLDS, FIRST_SENTENCE_HOLDS, HEADING_CASE and SUBJECT_FROM read one word each in
--       DECLARATIONS.md (subject, sentence, front_matter), and prosa.js reads any name there. They are names here, as
--       in the reference court. The menus kinds and measures record two closed vocabularies that no seat is typed by:
--       a kind is a DECLARATION and a measure is a seat of PROFILE.
--   S14 the decoder grammar: the forge writes HOLDS and DECLINES, two lists of references to a UNION of kinds, as one
--       name in prosa.gbnf. The court reads the list. The grammar holds the shape of every other clause.
--
-- MEASURED 2026-11-26 by haro/judge-prosa-court.js, on the forge of haro commit 989d6e6: the 66 fixtures of
-- conformance/manifest.json, each translated mechanically into the Commons shape and judged at level 2 by the court
-- forged from this file. 56 agree with prosa.js: all 50 declarations that are lawful at level 2 are judged clean, and
-- 6 of the 16 refused ones are refused under the same code (MISSING_FIELD, UNKNOWN_KIND, RULE_WITHOUT_EVIDENCE,
-- UNKNOWN_REFERENCE, ADOPTION_CYCLE, PIECE_WITHOUT_SUBJECT). 10 differ, and each is a named seam with one row in
-- haro/twin-expected.csv, which the judge enforces as a ratchet: 5 are refused under a code of the court (S7), and 5
-- are judged clean: a bound that is not a bound (S2), BOUND_INVERTED (S3), the two examples (S4) and
-- TERM_REFUSED_AND_REQUIRED (S5).

DEFINE LANGUAGE prosa AS (
  VERSION "0.1", GRAMMAR "0.1",
  COURT "conformance/manifest.json",
  EXTENSION ".proz"
) RATIONALE "What a written text owes its reader, declared before the text is judged: ten declaration kinds, a style and the rules it holds, a form, a piece bound to both, and every excuse with its reason"

-- ---- the closed vocabularies -----------------------------------------------------------

DEFINE MENU kinds AS (
  WORDS [style, term, wordlist, pattern, profile, form, zone, piece, allow, reading],
  MESSAGE "The kinds are closed: STYLE, TERM, WORDLIST, PATTERN, PROFILE, FORM, ZONE, PIECE, ALLOW, READING",
  CODE "UNKNOWN_KIND",
  CITES ["rule:UNKNOWN_KIND"]
) RATIONALE "STYLE groups rules; TERM, WORDLIST, PATTERN and PROFILE are the four kinds of rule; FORM declares a structure; ZONE and ALLOW excuse; PIECE binds a text; READING names a judgment that stays with a reader"

DEFINE MENU zones AS (
  WORDS [title, heading, lede, body, list, quote],
  MESSAGE "The value of IN is not lawful: zones are title, heading, lede, body, list, quote",
  CODE "BAD_VALUE",
  CITES ["rule:BAD_VALUE"]
) RATIONALE "Where a rule reads in a text; a rule with no IN reads lede, body, list and quote"

DEFINE MENU positions AS (
  WORDS [sentence_start, sentence_end, paragraph_start, paragraph_end],
  MESSAGE "The value of AT is not lawful: one of sentence_start, sentence_end, paragraph_start, paragraph_end",
  CODE "BAD_VALUE",
  CITES ["rule:BAD_VALUE"]
) RATIONALE "Where in a sentence or a paragraph a PATTERN is refused"

DEFINE MENU severities AS (
  WORDS [error, warning],
  MESSAGE "The value of SEVERITY is not lawful: error or warning is expected",
  CODE "BAD_VALUE",
  CITES ["rule:BAD_VALUE"]
) RATIONALE "A finding refuses or warns; TERM and PATTERN default to error, WORDLIST and PROFILE to warning"

DEFINE MENU measures AS (
  WORDS [sentence_median, sentences_over, sentences_under, dashes, colons, exclamations, cold_exclamations, questions, ellipses, colon_leads, one_sentence_paragraphs],
  MESSAGE "A measure of a PROFILE is one of: SENTENCE_MEDIAN, SENTENCES_OVER, SENTENCES_UNDER, DASHES, COLONS, EXCLAMATIONS, COLD_EXCLAMATIONS, QUESTIONS, ELLIPSES, COLON_LEADS, ONE_SENTENCE_PARAGRAPHS",
  CODE "UNKNOWN_FIELD",
  CITES ["rule:UNKNOWN_FIELD"]
) RATIONALE "The eleven measures of a voice; each is a seat of PROFILE and holds a bound"

DEFINE MENU mention_modes AS (
  WORDS [skipped, judged],
  MESSAGE "The value of MENTIONS is not lawful: skipped or judged is expected",
  CODE "BAD_VALUE",
  CITES ["rule:BAD_VALUE"]
) RATIONALE "A short quotation is a mention: skipped leaves it out, judged reads it as use"

-- ---- the forms: what a list holds --------------------------------------------------------

DEFINE FORM entry AS (
  SEATS [value: text]
) RATIONALE "One refused construction of REFUSES or MATCHES, with its WITHIN and its WRITE, as one text (S2)"

DEFINE FORM phrase AS (
  SEATS [value: text]
) RATIONALE "One word or phrase of KEEPS, HEADINGS or CLOSES_WITHOUT"

DEFINE FORM tongue AS (
  SEATS [value: name]
) RATIONALE "One language a style is written for: en, fr"

DEFINE FORM status AS (
  SEATS [value: name]
) RATIONALE "One status of the front matter at which a hole is refused: review, published"

DEFINE FORM excused AS (
  SEATS [value: name]
) RATIONALE "One code a zone excuses; a code is UPPER_SNAKE in a .proz file and lower_snake here"

DEFINE UNION rule AS (
  OF [term, wordlist, pattern, profile],
  MESSAGE "A rule seat names {value}, which is not a declared TERM or WORDLIST or PATTERN or PROFILE",
  CODE "UNKNOWN_REFERENCE",
  CITES ["rule:UNKNOWN_REFERENCE"]
) RATIONALE "The four kinds of rule a style holds or declines"

-- ---- the ten kinds ---------------------------------------------------------------------
-- A required seat carries no question mark, and its absence is MISSING_FIELD in the kind's own words. A seat typed by
-- a kind is a reference, and a name that resolves to nothing is UNKNOWN_REFERENCE. A seat that is both (FOLLOWS on
-- PIECE, ON on READING) is written optional with the reference's code, and a constraint speaks MISSING_FIELD.

DEFINE DECLARATION style AS (
  VERB "STYLE",
  SEATS [holds: [rule]?, adopts: [style]?, declines: [rule]?, languages: [tongue]?, measured_from: text?],
  MESSAGES [holds: "{name}: HOLDS names {value}, which is not a declared TERM or WORDLIST or PATTERN or PROFILE", adopts: "{name}: ADOPTS names {value}, which is not a declared STYLE", declines: "{name}: DECLINES names {value}, which is not a declared TERM or WORDLIST or PATTERN or PROFILE"],
  CODES [holds: "UNKNOWN_REFERENCE", adopts: "UNKNOWN_REFERENCE", declines: "UNKNOWN_REFERENCE"]
) RATIONALE "A named set of rules: the voice of a house, or a set a house adopts. Its rules are those it holds, with those of every style it adopts, less those it declines"

DEFINE DECLARATION term AS (
  VERB "TERM",
  SEATS [means: text, refuses: [entry]?, writes: text?, evidence: text?, code: name?, severity: severities?, language: name?, on: [form]?, in: [zones]?, mentions: mention_modes?, keeps: [phrase]?, says: text?],
  MESSAGES [means: "{name}: TERM needs the field MEANS", on: "{name}: ON names {value}, which is not a declared FORM"],
  CODES [means: "MISSING_FIELD", on: "UNKNOWN_REFERENCE"]
) RATIONALE "One thing has one word: the house word, what it means, and the words refused in its place"

DEFINE DECLARATION wordlist AS (
  VERB "WORDLIST",
  SEATS [refuses: [entry]?, at_most: text?, evidence: text?, code: name, severity: severities?, language: name?, on: [form]?, in: [zones]?, mentions: mention_modes?, keeps: [phrase]?, says: text?],
  MESSAGES [code: "{name}: WORDLIST needs the field CODE", on: "{name}: ON names {value}, which is not a declared FORM"],
  CODES [code: "MISSING_FIELD", on: "UNKNOWN_REFERENCE"]
) RATIONALE "A list of refused words and phrases, each finding by itself or the whole list under a budget"

DEFINE DECLARATION pattern AS (
  VERB "PATTERN",
  SEATS [matches: [entry]?, at: positions?, refused: text?, written: text?, at_most: text?, evidence: text?, code: name, severity: severities?, language: name?, on: [form]?, in: [zones]?, mentions: mention_modes?, keeps: [phrase]?, says: text?],
  MESSAGES [code: "{name}: PATTERN needs the field CODE", on: "{name}: ON names {value}, which is not a declared FORM"],
  CODES [code: "MISSING_FIELD", on: "UNKNOWN_REFERENCE"]
) RATIONALE "A refused construction, at a position when one is given, with the examples that test it"

DEFINE DECLARATION profile AS (
  VERB "PROFILE",
  SEATS [sentence_median: text?, sentences_over: text?, sentences_under: text?, dashes: text?, colons: text?, exclamations: text?, cold_exclamations: text?, questions: text?, ellipses: text?, colon_leads: text?, one_sentence_paragraphs: text?, min_words: number?, evidence: text?, code: name?, severity: severities?, language: name?, on: [form]?],
  MESSAGES [on: "{name}: ON names {value}, which is not a declared FORM"],
  CODES [on: "UNKNOWN_REFERENCE"]
) RATIONALE "The measure of a voice: each measure a bound, silent on a text shorter than MIN_WORDS"

DEFINE DECLARATION form AS (
  VERB "FORM",
  SEATS [extends: form?, title_words: text?, title_holds: name?, first_sentence_holds: name?, say_once: text?, headings: [phrase]?, heading_case: name?, closes_without: [phrase]?, holes_closed_at: [status]?, evidence: text?],
  MESSAGES [extends: "{name}: EXTENDS names {value}, which is not a declared FORM"],
  CODES [extends: "UNKNOWN_REFERENCE"]
) RATIONALE "The structure of a kind of text: its title, its first sentence, its headings and its close"

DEFINE DECLARATION zone AS (
  VERB "ZONE",
  SEATS [exempt_from: [excused]?, reason: text],
  MESSAGES [reason: "{name}: ZONE needs the field REASON"],
  CODES [reason: "MISSING_FIELD"]
) RATIONALE "A region of a text excused from named codes, with a reason"

DEFINE DECLARATION piece AS (
  VERB "PIECE",
  SEATS [file: text?, files: text?, follows: style?, form: form?, subject: text?, subject_from: name?, language: name?, reader: text?],
  MESSAGES [follows: "{name}: FOLLOWS names {value}, which is not a declared STYLE", form: "{name}: FORM names {value}, which is not a declared FORM"],
  CODES [follows: "UNKNOWN_REFERENCE", form: "UNKNOWN_REFERENCE"]
) RATIONALE "One text bound to a style and a form"

DEFINE DECLARATION allow AS (
  VERB "ALLOW",
  SEATS [file: text, line_holds: text, excuses: name, reason: text],
  MESSAGES [file: "{name}: ALLOW needs the field FILE", line_holds: "{name}: ALLOW needs the field LINE_HOLDS", excuses: "{name}: ALLOW needs the field EXCUSES", reason: "{name}: ALLOW needs the field REASON"],
  CODES [file: "MISSING_FIELD", line_holds: "MISSING_FIELD", excuses: "MISSING_FIELD", reason: "MISSING_FIELD"]
) RATIONALE "One line of one file excused from one code, with a reason"

DEFINE DECLARATION reading AS (
  VERB "READING",
  SEATS [on: form?, asks: text, records: text, evidence: text?],
  MESSAGES [on: "{name}: ON names {value}, which is not a declared FORM", asks: "{name}: READING needs the field ASKS", records: "{name}: READING needs the field RECORDS"],
  CODES [on: "UNKNOWN_REFERENCE", asks: "MISSING_FIELD", records: "MISSING_FIELD"]
) RATIONALE "A judgment that stays with a reader, human or AI model: a question, and where its records stand"

-- ---- the court: level 1, what a required seat does not say -------------------------------
-- Each constraint states the OFFENCE as its WHEN and speaks the diagnostic code as its CODE. The MESSAGE is the
-- summary of violations.json with its fields filled in; CITES names the diagnostic (S11).

DEFINE CONSTRAINT missing_refuses_term AS (
  ON term, WHEN "refuses absent",
  MESSAGE "{name}: TERM needs the field REFUSES",
  CODE "MISSING_FIELD",
  CITES ["rule:MISSING_FIELD"]
) RATIONALE "A declaration carries its required fields. REFUSES is a list, so the seat is optional and this constraint asks for it; level 1"

DEFINE CONSTRAINT missing_refuses_wordlist AS (
  ON wordlist, WHEN "refuses absent",
  MESSAGE "{name}: WORDLIST needs the field REFUSES",
  CODE "MISSING_FIELD",
  CITES ["rule:MISSING_FIELD"]
) RATIONALE "A declaration carries its required fields. REFUSES is a list, so the seat is optional and this constraint asks for it; level 1"

DEFINE CONSTRAINT missing_matches_pattern AS (
  ON pattern, WHEN "matches absent",
  MESSAGE "{name}: PATTERN needs the field MATCHES",
  CODE "MISSING_FIELD",
  CITES ["rule:MISSING_FIELD"]
) RATIONALE "A declaration carries its required fields. MATCHES is a list, so the seat is optional and this constraint asks for it; level 1"

DEFINE CONSTRAINT missing_exempt_from_zone AS (
  ON zone, WHEN "exempt_from absent",
  MESSAGE "{name}: ZONE needs the field EXEMPT_FROM",
  CODE "MISSING_FIELD",
  CITES ["rule:MISSING_FIELD"]
) RATIONALE "A declaration carries its required fields. EXEMPT_FROM is a list, so the seat is optional and this constraint asks for it; level 1"

DEFINE CONSTRAINT missing_follows_piece AS (
  ON piece, WHEN "follows absent",
  MESSAGE "{name}: PIECE needs the field FOLLOWS",
  CODE "MISSING_FIELD",
  CITES ["rule:MISSING_FIELD"]
) RATIONALE "A declaration carries its required fields. FOLLOWS is a reference, so the seat is optional and this constraint asks for it; level 1"

DEFINE CONSTRAINT missing_on_reading AS (
  ON reading, WHEN "on absent",
  MESSAGE "{name}: READING needs the field ON",
  CODE "MISSING_FIELD",
  CITES ["rule:MISSING_FIELD"]
) RATIONALE "A declaration carries its required fields. ON is a reference, so the seat is optional and this constraint asks for it; level 1"

DEFINE CONSTRAINT piece_file_or_files AS (
  ON piece, WHEN "(file absent and files absent) or (file present and files present)",
  MESSAGE "{name}: PIECE needs the field FILE or FILES (one of the two)",
  CODE "MISSING_FIELD",
  CITES ["rule:MISSING_FIELD"]
) RATIONALE "A piece declares FILE or FILES, one of the two; level 1"

-- ---- the court: level 2, the declaration by itself ----------------------------------------

DEFINE CONSTRAINT rule_without_evidence_term AS (
  ON term, WHEN "evidence absent",
  MESSAGE "{name}: This TERM carries no EVIDENCE: a rule enters on a dated ruling or a measure",
  CODE "RULE_WITHOUT_EVIDENCE",
  CITES ["rule:RULE_WITHOUT_EVIDENCE"]
) RATIONALE "Every rule cites the ruling or the measure it comes from.; level 2"

DEFINE CONSTRAINT rule_without_evidence_wordlist AS (
  ON wordlist, WHEN "evidence absent",
  MESSAGE "{name}: This WORDLIST carries no EVIDENCE: a rule enters on a dated ruling or a measure",
  CODE "RULE_WITHOUT_EVIDENCE",
  CITES ["rule:RULE_WITHOUT_EVIDENCE"]
) RATIONALE "Every rule cites the ruling or the measure it comes from.; level 2"

DEFINE CONSTRAINT rule_without_evidence_pattern AS (
  ON pattern, WHEN "evidence absent",
  MESSAGE "{name}: This PATTERN carries no EVIDENCE: a rule enters on a dated ruling or a measure",
  CODE "RULE_WITHOUT_EVIDENCE",
  CITES ["rule:RULE_WITHOUT_EVIDENCE"]
) RATIONALE "Every rule cites the ruling or the measure it comes from.; level 2"

DEFINE CONSTRAINT rule_without_evidence_profile AS (
  ON profile, WHEN "evidence absent",
  MESSAGE "{name}: This PROFILE carries no EVIDENCE: a rule enters on a dated ruling or a measure",
  CODE "RULE_WITHOUT_EVIDENCE",
  CITES ["rule:RULE_WITHOUT_EVIDENCE"]
) RATIONALE "Every rule cites the ruling or the measure it comes from.; level 2"

DEFINE CONSTRAINT rule_without_evidence_form AS (
  ON form, WHEN "evidence absent",
  MESSAGE "{name}: This FORM carries no EVIDENCE: a rule enters on a dated ruling or a measure",
  CODE "RULE_WITHOUT_EVIDENCE",
  CITES ["rule:RULE_WITHOUT_EVIDENCE"]
) RATIONALE "Every rule cites the ruling or the measure it comes from.; level 2"

DEFINE CONSTRAINT adoption_cycle_style AS (
  ON style, WHEN "adopts cyclic",
  MESSAGE "{name}: ADOPTS leads back to this declaration",
  CODE "ADOPTION_CYCLE",
  CITES ["rule:ADOPTION_CYCLE"]
) RATIONALE "Adoption and extension form no cycle.; level 2"

DEFINE CONSTRAINT adoption_cycle_form AS (
  ON form, WHEN "extends = self or extends.extends = self or extends.extends.extends = self",
  MESSAGE "{name}: EXTENDS leads back to this declaration",
  CODE "ADOPTION_CYCLE",
  CITES ["rule:ADOPTION_CYCLE"]
) RATIONALE "Adoption and extension form no cycle. EXTENDS holds one name, and cyclic reads a list, so three steps are written out (S6); level 2"

DEFINE CONSTRAINT piece_without_subject AS (
  ON piece, WHEN "form present and subject absent and subject_from absent and (form.title_holds present or form.first_sentence_holds present or form.extends.title_holds present or form.extends.first_sentence_holds present)",
  MESSAGE "{name}: The form {form} places the subject, and the piece declares no SUBJECT",
  CODE "PIECE_WITHOUT_SUBJECT",
  CITES ["rule:PIECE_WITHOUT_SUBJECT"]
) RATIONALE "A piece whose form places the subject declares it. Two steps of EXTENDS are read (S6); level 2"

-- ---- the refusals ----------------------------------------------------------------------

DEFINE REFUSAL unknown_verb AS (
  MESSAGE "A Prosa declaration is DEFINE <KIND> <name> ( ... ); nothing else opens a declaration.",
  CODE "UNEXPECTED_TOKEN",
  CITES ["rule:UNEXPECTED_TOKEN"]
) RATIONALE "A .proz file is a sequence of USE lines and DEFINE declarations."

DEFINE REFUSAL unknown_declaration AS (
  MESSAGE "The kinds are closed: STYLE, TERM, WORDLIST, PATTERN, PROFILE, FORM, ZONE, PIECE, ALLOW, READING.",
  CODE "UNKNOWN_KIND",
  CITES ["rule:UNKNOWN_KIND"]
) RATIONALE "A kind outside the ten is refused by name: a declared language refuses what it does not know"

